regarding wishing, polymorph loopholes and so on:

* you should never be able to wish for a wish (blessed magic lamps should
    be inactive, wish wands have no charges and can't be recharged, etc).

* polymorph ought to be able to shock inanimate systems and occasionally
    destroy them, thus making "stash" re-rolling less feasible. a 5%
    chance of object shock is doable.

* fountains should only "cancel" uncursed magic. blessed magic could
    become uncursed by dipping and similarly with cursed magic.
currently in nethack 3.0 there is a point you reach such that when you get
the wand of polymorph and you use it to get more desirable magic the process
becomes unstable and actually diverges. you can end up with many wands of
wishing and polymorph and, in addition, all the advantageous magic you desire.
there is no skill required in playing a wish-at-will game. perhaps certain
intelligent monsters should start wielding Stormbringers in their defense
and casting real spells (i.e. cancellation) and also teleport willfully, see
invisible and so on when you get to Xp=20, AC=-20, Hp=200, etc.. that would
start to justify the current situation where you can enjoy outrageous
advantages (if you're clever). oh yeah, the Amulet of Yendor should fix
your AC to -20 regardless of what it was before and should be "bagable" and
The Wizard should be able to steal that entire container ...

